ENVIRONMENT
-----------
- .NET SDK 10.0.300 present; WinUI 3 / Windows App SDK 2.1.0 build works (full
  solution builds clean). The Windows runner IS available, so the gate is NOT
  blocked.
- The generated C# OpenAPI client (apps/windows/Generated/, namespace
  TeslaSync.Windows.Generated.Api) is .gitignored + regenerated, not committed.
  Regenerated via `npx --yes tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts`
  (10 C# files) and materialized apps/windows/Generated/Generated.csproj so the
  two project references (Core + Tests) resolve. All four api-keys operations are
  present in ApiEndpoints.cs:
    get_api_v1_api_keys            GET    /api-keys/
    post_api_v1_api_keys           POST   /api-keys/
    delete_api_v1_api_keys_id      DELETE /api-keys/{id}/
    post_api_v1_api_keys_id_revoke POST   /api-keys/{id}/revoke

PATH / OUTPUT RECONCILIATION (no scope narrowing)
-------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names `apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/APIKeysPage.xaml`
+ `APIKeysPageViewModel.cs`. That path/shape does not exist in this repo: every
shipped W7 page (ApiLogsPage, ApiPlaygroundPage, WebhooksPage, …) lives under
`apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Page>/` and is authored as **C# markup**
(no per-page .xaml) split into <Page>.cs / .Model.cs / .ViewModel.cs / .Source.cs
in namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin. The prompt's literal path is
generated boilerplate; the page was implemented following the real, established
convention so it integrates with the W3 component library, the W4 shell and the
P1/S8 state-holder seam exactly like its peers.

